# Omni-Changeling: Convoke (CR 702.51) lets Bot1 tap three Ornithopters (two of them summoning sick: convoke ignores that, the ruling) to pay
# {3}, and Mox Sapphire and an Island pay {U}{U}. As it enters, "you may have this creature enter as a copy of any creature on the
# battlefield, except it has changeling" (CR 614.1c, 707.2, 707.9b): the choice is accepted and the copied creature is an Ornithopter,
# so the permanent is a 0/2 Ornithopter with flying, and with changeling it is every creature type (CR 702.73a), where the
# Ornithopters it copied are only Thopters. It does not die as a 0/0. The three Ornithopters stay tapped.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Mox Sapphire
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Omni-Changeling
Island
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Island.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Omni-Changeling.Cast(Convoke: Ornithopter, Ornithopter, Ornithopter)
Bot1.Accept
Bot1.Target(Ornithopter#1)
Bot2.Pass
[Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Tapped = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#3.Tapped = true

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#4.Power = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#4.Toughness = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#4.Keywords = Changeling; Flying
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#4.Subtypes = (every creature type)
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#4.Types = Artifact; Creature
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#4.Colors = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
